# Case: Native clipboard holder and excluded-tag cleanup
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Verify managed received files and native clipboard leases under unified cleanup.
# Steps:
#   Pair an owned production peer; receive a synthetic user file onto the real clipboard; enable count cleanup with an excluded tag; remove the exclusion; replace the clipboard.
# Expected:
#   Exclusion protects history and file; removing it deletes eligible history but preserves the held native file; replacing the clipboard reclaims only the managed file and preserves the original source.
# Forbidden:
#   Directory fixtures, deleting a user-owned source, treating history deletion as holder release, or claims of two graphical endpoints.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D managed cleanup baseline'
start
ui-click listItem 设置…
ui-wait listItem 同步
ui-click listItem 同步
ui-enabled switch 启用同步
ui-click switch 启用同步
config-equals sync.enabled true
connect-policy-peer
system-file-cleanup
screenshot native-holder-released
